    "limitations": "Bounded customer-neutral pin editing, exact OR tag exclusions and allowed rendering-type constraints only. No customer vocabulary/aliases, lists/default assets, priority/multi-position policy or full W20/F28/F26/customer acceptance. Literal explicit tags are preserved; only absent contentType uses the existing safe render-kind fallback identically on every arm. Rendering types remain distinct from format-affinity tags. Old stored unversioned/v1 parsing and absent/v1 receipt meanings remain; new v2 is explicit. No migration/history rewrite, scoring/model/SDK/service/cache/store/auth change. Existing30-second cache, independent catalog/slot revisions and non-atomic publication remain; catalog-dependent pin feedback advisory with authoritative runtime refusal and no arbitrary fill. Old v1 readers reject v2 documents, but mixed old cached readers remain possible: compatible readers/UI before controlled publication; no immediate rollout/native/SLO/default-rendering proof. W20.03 prior exact-byte evidence is prospectively qualified with implemented controls/history retained; W08.04 unchanged. No deploy/cloud/build/install/provision/seed/credentials/customer-data/destructive/commit/push/external operations. No package/finding/gate/release promotion.",
